hat examines the urine's physical, chemical, and microscopic properties, providing a broad overview of the urinary system's health. It can detect a range of issues, from kidney and liver disorders to diabetes and urinary tract infections (UTIs), depending on the findings such as the presence of proteins, glucose, red and white blood cells, and bacteria.\n\nOn the other hand, a urine culture is a more targeted test that specifically identifies and quantifies the types of bacteria present in the urine. This test is particularly useful in diagnosing urinary tract infections (UTIs), determining the causative agent, and guiding appropriate antibiotic treatment. It is usually performed when a UTI is suspected based on symptoms or abnormal findings in urinalysis, and the results can inform the choice of antibiotics to ensure effective treatment.	2026-06-06 21:31:41.255081
