actors, such as a high A1C level, should medication be considered. (Source: 4. Comprehensive Medical Evaluation and Assessment of Comorbidities: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2024.pdf, Pág: 4)\n\nReferring the patient to a cardiologist without attempting lifestyle modifications first is also not the most appropriate next step. This would be a more drastic measure and may not be necessary at this stage, given that the patient does not have any other concerning risk factors or symptoms. (Source: 4. Comprehensive Medical Evaluation and Assessment of Comorbidities: Standards of Care in Diabetes—2024.pdf, Pág: 4)\n\nRepeating the fasting laboratory studies in 1 month is	2026-06-06 23:46:51.342223
