ressure: Although the patient's blood pressure is also elevated (156/98 mm Hg), the primary focus should be on managing his LDL-cholesterol concentration, as indicated by his family history and current cholesterol levels.\n\n(E) Suppressing appetite: There is no indication that suppressing appetite is the most appropriate pharmacotherapy approach based on the given clinical context and patient's condition.\n\n\nQuestion:\nQuestion: Which of the following best describes the clinical management approach for a patient with chronic coronary heart disease (CHD) and chronic kidney disease (CKD) based on the evidence provided?\n\n--- Fragmento (Fonte: 2023-04-07.pdf, Página 1) ---\n\n--- Fragmento 2.\n\n--- Fragmento 2023-04-	2026-06-07 11:29:31.957951
