ment during an acute crisis.\n\nD: Iron supplementation is typically used for iron-deficiency anemia and is not indicated in sickle cell anemia, which is not related to iron deficiency but to the abnormal hemoglobin.\n\nHence, the most appropriate choice is E, Transfusion of packed red blood cells, to immediately address the patient's acute anemia and symptoms.\n\n\n# Response: E\n\n\n- [support]: E\n\n\n\nExplanation\n===\nThe patient's symptoms and laboratory results suggest she is in an acute sickle cell crisis with anemia. Sickle cell crisis management would include treating symptoms and complications of sickle cell disease. A:\n===\n\n=== fragment \n===\n=== Fragment \n=== Fragment \n=== DETAILS === Fragment \n=== Fragment \n=== Fragment \n=== Fragment \n=== Fragment \n=== Fragment \n=== Fragment \n=== Fragment \n===	2026-06-07 11:48:52.151339
