ient, who has a history of CCD and concerns about life-threatening VTE.\n\n(B) Surgical ligation of the largest veins: Surgical ligation of the largest veins is not a recommended treatment for VTE, especially in the absence of a clear indication for surgery.\n\n(C) Venography: Venography is an invasive imaging modality that is not necessary for evaluating VTE in this patient, who has a history of CCD and concerns about life-threatening VTE.\n\n(E) Warfarin therapy: Warfarin therapy is not the most appropriate next step in this patient, who has a history of CCD and concerns about life-threatening VTE. Warfarin therapy may increase the risk of bleeding complications in patients with CCD.\n\nIn conclusion, the most appropriate next step for this patient is to perform venous duplex ultrasonography to evaluate for VTE and underlying vasculopathies in other vascular beds.	2026-06-07 12:38:06.774775
